# The one file a user needs. Installing it adds the remote and installs the
# extension in a single step, and from then on `flatpak update` brings new
# versions along with everything else -- which a downloaded bundle does not.
#
# Url is where the repository is served from. The default below is GitHub Pages
# for this project's own repository; change it if it is hosted elsewhere.
#
# GPGKey is the repository's signing key, exported and base64-encoded. Without
# it `flatpak` marks the remote `no-gpg-verify` and takes whatever the server
# hands it, quietly. The private half lives only on the release machine;
# `flatpak build-update-repo --gpg-sign=` is what signs with it.
[Flatpak Ref]
